The existing models they compared with are:

- Syn Dep, OpenIE, and SRL (neural semantic parsing models based on Stanford dependencies, open information extraction, and semantic role labeling, respectively);
- BiDAF, QANet, and BERT (traditional MRC models);
- NAQANet and NAQANet+ (numerical MRC models).

The core components identified for training VQA models are:

(i) Pre-trained word embeddings, recurrent sentence encoders, and transformer-based sentence encoders as question representation strategies;  
(ii) Distinct convolutional neural networks (e.g., VGG-16, ResNet-101) used for visual feature extraction;  
(iii) Standard fusion strategies and the importance of two main attention mechanisms (specifically, Top-Down attention is highlighted as preferred).

These components are systematically tested to understand their individual impact on the final performance of VQA models.
